From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: don't wait for vblank on a slave video encoder

dpu_encoder_phys_vid_wait_for_commit_done() waits for pending_kickoff_cnt
to reach zero, which only the vblank irq does. Slave encoders of a bonded
display never enable that irq, while _dpu_encoder_trigger_flush() still
counts every kickoff on them. On the dual-DSI TB321FU every commit that
waited for the flush timed out on the slave after 50 ms ("vblank
timeout: 0", about ten a second in Game Mode).

Wait for the flush register alone on a slave; the master still waits for
its vblank irq.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -616,10 +616,15 @@
 	 * irq has run: with AVR a commit made during a held front porch starts
 	 * its frame at once, and 37 of 2700 flips went out with the previous
 	 * frame's count and time.
+	 *
+	 * A slave of a bonded display has no vblank irq, so its count never
+	 * goes down: it waits for the flush register only, like in
+	 * wait_for_tx_complete.
 	 */
 	ret = wait_event_timeout(phys_enc->pending_kickoff_wq,
 		(hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register(hw_ctl) == 0 &&
-		 atomic_read(&phys_enc->pending_kickoff_cnt) == 0),
+		 (!dpu_encoder_phys_vid_is_master(phys_enc) ||
+		  atomic_read(&phys_enc->pending_kickoff_cnt) == 0)),
 		msecs_to_jiffies(50));
 	if (ret <= 0) {
 		DPU_ERROR("vblank timeout: %x\n", hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register(hw_ctl));
